# LemAstra gitleaks fingerprint allowlist (GATE-06).
#
# CONTRACT — binding for every entry added to this file
# (authority: docs/governance/secret-isolation-policy.md §3):
#
#   1. Every fingerprint line MUST be preceded by two comment lines:
#        # class: publishable-identifier   <- the only class that may be allowlisted
#        # rationale: <what the identifier is and why it is safe to ship>
#      (e.g. Supabase publishable key with RLS-enforced authorization, Sentry DSN,
#      API endpoint URL — see the policy's classification table).
#   2. Entries claiming any other class (secret, user secret) are INVALID and
#      must be rejected in review — that is allowlist abuse (threat T-01-11).
#   3. An unannotated fingerprint is a gate violation, not a style issue:
#      silent ignores destroy the scanner's signal.
#
# There are currently ZERO fingerprint entries — no publishable identifier is
# in the client yet (Supabase/Sentry arrive in later phases). When the first
# real identifier is added, append its fingerprint below the required
# class + rationale comment pair.
